WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:03.230
Didn't I Say to Make My Abilities 
Average in the Next Life?!

00:00:06.350 --> 00:00:09.230
It's about an hour to the next town.

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.810
Are you tired, Reina?

00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.840
I'm completely fine!

00:00:13.840 --> 00:00:15.310
Is that so?

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:18.100
Stop it, Dad!

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:18.100
You're such a good girl, Reina.

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:23.250
Since before I could remember, I traveled
 with my father, who was a peddler.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:27.500
I had no memories of my mother, 
and you couldn't call us wealthy, but...

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:31.820
My life with my gentle father 
was a very happy one.

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.600
Don't worry. I'm here with you.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:44.010
Hey, Boss, there's nothing 
worth anything here.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:46.180
Making us go through this for nothing?

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:47.960
But, well...

00:00:47.960 --> 00:00:51.020
This little piece of merchandise 
should make us some money.

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:52.480
Reina!

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:53.730
Dad!

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:54.860
Hey, now...

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:56.820
Please! Anything but my daughter!

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:58.180
Don't worry.

00:00:58.760 --> 00:00:59.800
Hup.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:04.330
I'll sell her to a master who'll 
take real good care of her.

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.210
Reina! Reina!

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.650
Quit your yelling.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.440
Do it.

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:09.440
Reina!

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:10.660
You got it.

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:16.220
See? It's nice and quiet now.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:25.300
Dad?

00:01:26.040 --> 00:01:28.450
Uh-oh. You traumatized now?

00:01:30.120 --> 00:01:31.520
Hunters!

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:35.810
Dad!

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:37.320
Dad! Dad!

00:01:37.630 --> 00:01:40.030
Dad!

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:46.460
<b>Episode 5
Didn't I Say That We're Doing Everyone's Backstories?!</b>

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.040
That was ten years ago.

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.830
And, having lost my father, I...

00:01:52.210 --> 00:01:56.550
I'm sorry. If we'd only passed 
through here a little sooner...

00:02:05.050 --> 00:02:06.770
Do you want to come with us?

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:15.160
The Hunters who saved me, the 
Crimson Lightning, took me in.

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:20.230
Fireball!

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:22.740
Hey! We said to stay hidden!

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.080
Fireball!

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:26.540
Well, now...

00:02:28.090 --> 00:02:30.950
What do you think, Reina? 
It's a staff just like mine.

00:02:30.950 --> 00:02:32.710
Thank you, August!

00:02:32.940 --> 00:02:36.050
Though it's still a little 
big for you, Reina.

00:02:36.050 --> 00:02:39.540
Reina-chan, why don't you come sit 
on your big brother's lap sometimes?

00:02:39.540 --> 00:02:41.910
No one wants to sit on a filthy guy's lap.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.300
Right, Reina?

00:02:43.640 --> 00:02:45.480
What's that supposed to mean, August?

00:02:45.480 --> 00:02:47.420
Stop keeping Reina all to yourself!

00:02:47.420 --> 00:02:50.210
All of us pitched in to pay 
for that staff, you know!

00:02:50.210 --> 00:02:51.940
Pipe down. No one asked you.

00:02:52.250 --> 00:02:53.800
Fireball!

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.140
Nice work. Just like that.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.790
Fireball!

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.720
Almost!

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:06.260
Real combat's still a ways off.

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:07.540
What?

00:03:08.070 --> 00:03:10.530
Gather, Water! Come to me!

00:03:10.530 --> 00:03:12.030
Form a water ball!

00:03:14.120 --> 00:03:15.050
Thank you.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.960
Reina, your birthday's coming up, right?

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.230
That's right.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:21.770
So Reina's going to be ten, huh?

00:03:21.770 --> 00:03:23.520
Is there anything you want?

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:24.870
You can ask for anything.

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:26.850
I... Um...

00:03:26.850 --> 00:03:30.810
I've always thought your 
choker looked cool, August...

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:31.990
You can't have this.

00:03:31.990 --> 00:03:32.560
Huh?

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.200
You said I could ask for anything!

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:37.630
You don't have boobs yet and 
you're trying to be sexy?

00:03:37.630 --> 00:03:40.110
I'm gonna get bigger than you, August!

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.030
If you think you can, go ahead and try!

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.080
Come on!

00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:44.220
Now, now. Don't fight.

00:03:45.740 --> 00:03:47.350
Honestly!

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:52.290
This is a memento of 
my mother, who passed away.

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:54.500
Huh? Really?

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.300
I'm so sorry, I—

00:03:56.940 --> 00:03:59.700
I'd really like it if you'd accept it, Reina.

00:04:01.650 --> 00:04:04.470
They gave me everything.

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:07.720
They had no responsibility 
or obligation to do it.

00:04:07.720 --> 00:04:09.980
They were simply really good people.

00:04:12.280 --> 00:04:16.190
One day, we'd agreed to guard 
a caravan of merchants.

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:17.360
And then...

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:21.260
We were attacked by bandits in numbers 
far too great for us to defeat.

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:25.820
Our Guild contract acknowledged 
surrender as an option.

00:04:26.490 --> 00:04:28.730
And bandits, fearing reprisals from the Guild,

00:04:28.730 --> 00:04:31.070
might take our goods, but they
 wouldn't take our lives.

00:04:31.710 --> 00:04:32.640
But...

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:35.080
Shall we make a trade?

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:40.920
Huh? What do you plan to offer 
this late in the game?

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.000
In exchange for half our cargo,

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.590
what do you think of a little girl 
who can use magic to make water?

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:47.510
What?

00:04:47.880 --> 00:04:50.260
We were betrayed by the man who'd hired us.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.100
You can't be serious! 
That violates our agreement!

00:04:53.100 --> 00:04:56.360
He's right. The Guild wouldn't stand for that.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.810
That's only if they find out, right?

00:05:00.720 --> 00:05:02.190
I see.

00:05:02.620 --> 00:05:06.320
As long as she lives, she'll serve as 
a water barrel that never runs dry.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.070
I think she'd be useful 
for any number of things.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:13.260
Guys, I don't want a scratch 
on the little girl.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:14.960
Get 'em!

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:20.890
O Flames, form a wall around me!

00:05:20.890 --> 00:05:21.960
Fire Shield!

00:05:23.980 --> 00:05:26.440
O Flames, form a wall around me!

00:05:26.440 --> 00:05:28.840
O Flames, form a wall around me!

00:05:28.840 --> 00:05:31.460
O Flames, form a wall around—

00:05:33.270 --> 00:05:35.220
I'm sorry... Reina...

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.170
But, man, you guys are pretty cruel.

00:05:48.170 --> 00:05:50.490
Killing all the people you hired.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:58.250
Blaze brightly, righteous fires of Hell!

00:06:00.670 --> 00:06:01.680
The girl!

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.310
What is all this?

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:05.910
She can't! She's not done training yet!

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.300
Hey! Guys!

00:06:07.470 --> 00:06:09.510
Burn them to ash!

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:13.970
B-Boss!

00:06:14.750 --> 00:06:15.970
Wh-What's that?

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.600
It's the guard! Run!

00:06:19.110 --> 00:06:23.370
That day, the me that had everything 
precious stolen from her died,

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:26.690
and Crimson Reina was born.

00:06:27.330 --> 00:06:29.030
I see.

00:06:29.030 --> 00:06:29.820
That's it?

00:06:30.020 --> 00:06:31.410
Wha? That's really all?

00:06:31.670 --> 00:06:34.520
Oh. Would it be better if we said something?

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:36.630
Like, "Nothing good comes from revenge," or

00:06:36.630 --> 00:06:40.080
"Do you think that's what the people 
who died would have wanted?"

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:40.830
Wha?

00:06:40.830 --> 00:06:42.000
Or perhaps...

00:06:42.000 --> 00:06:45.460
you'd prefer if we reacted like that?

00:06:45.720 --> 00:06:46.550
Huh?

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.700
R-R-Reina!

00:06:52.700 --> 00:06:54.680
It m-must have been so hard...

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:55.720
Huh?

00:06:55.720 --> 00:06:57.830
Reina!

00:06:57.830 --> 00:06:59.550
Come cry in my bosom!

00:06:59.550 --> 00:07:01.480
Help me, you two!

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:04.730
Do you have hearts of stone or something?

00:07:04.910 --> 00:07:07.120
Okay! Okay, I get it!

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.130
Thank you, Mavis!

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:13.920
At any rate! It's only a matter of course 
that thieves and evildoers should die!

00:07:13.920 --> 00:07:14.620
That's why...

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:17.150
You were trying to have us fight...

00:07:17.150 --> 00:07:20.500
no, kill people, right?

00:07:20.770 --> 00:07:24.460
That's right. If you don't kill bad guys 
when you have the chance, they'll just—

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:26.080
I refuse.

00:07:26.080 --> 00:07:26.960
What?

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:30.840
I understand why Reina 
hates villains and bandits.

00:07:31.230 --> 00:07:35.220
But we can't take the thoughts of an 
individual as the policy of the party.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.570
As long as we're Hunters, I do 
think that day will come someday.

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:40.720
But...

00:07:40.720 --> 00:07:44.770
I don't think practicing killing people
 is the right way to go about this.

00:07:45.060 --> 00:07:47.010
How can you be so naïve?

00:07:47.010 --> 00:07:49.880
It's because you don't understand how it feels

00:07:49.880 --> 00:07:51.900
to have your family stolen 
from you like I do!

00:07:52.060 --> 00:07:54.890
Oh! In that case, want to hear?

00:07:54.890 --> 00:07:56.160
About my past.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:57.100
Huh?

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.620
The Beckett Company of Talwess is a company 
you may or may not have heard of.

00:08:04.120 --> 00:08:08.780
Surrounded by honest, kind parents 
and a very young little brother,

00:08:08.780 --> 00:08:11.940
I lived a life free of any want or discomfort.

00:08:12.560 --> 00:08:14.380
But one day...

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:19.220
Thieves broke into the Company, 
and my father alone was killed.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:22.070
We were lost in our grief.

00:08:22.070 --> 00:08:24.130
The head clerk thrust upon us...

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:27.610
a deed he said my father had left,

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:29.650
transferring the business to him.

00:08:30.180 --> 00:08:31.200
It was impossible.

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:35.180
But the local lord supported 
the head clerk's claims.

00:08:35.180 --> 00:08:37.160
My father's business was stolen,

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:40.540
and the head clerk pressed my 
mother to become his mistress.

00:08:41.030 --> 00:08:42.120
And then...

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:44.120
Why that man?

00:08:44.360 --> 00:08:47.130
He killed Father! I'm sure of it!

00:08:47.130 --> 00:08:50.060
My role as your father's wife has ended.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.490
All that's left is to be a mother 
and make sure you grow up well.

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:58.010
When that's done...

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:03.520
I'll become his wife once more, 
and fulfill my final duty.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:09.420
There's no need for that.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:14.400
As his daughter, I'll fulfill that duty.

00:09:14.720 --> 00:09:17.560
In search of power, 
I aimed to become a Hunter,

00:09:18.040 --> 00:09:19.740
and met all of you!

00:09:19.980 --> 00:09:22.660
A child of strife is strife itself, they say...

00:09:25.490 --> 00:09:27.520
<i>Terrifying! Truly terrifying!</i>

00:09:27.520 --> 00:09:29.920
<i>That smile of Pauline's!</i>

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:33.120
Now, it's Mavis's turn, right?

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:33.880
What?

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:35.130
Wh-Why?

00:09:35.800 --> 00:09:37.320
Since we have the opportunity,

00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:40.260
I thought it might be easier on everyone 
if we got everything out in the open.

00:09:40.260 --> 00:09:44.020
It's true. The reason why Mavis-san 
chose to become a Hunter...

00:09:44.020 --> 00:09:46.260
I'd really like to know!

00:09:47.000 --> 00:09:50.120
Stare...

00:09:50.120 --> 00:09:52.020
O-Okay! I get it!

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:55.950
I was born as the eldest 
daughter of Count Austien.

00:09:56.680 --> 00:09:58.960
I lost my mother early,

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:03.040
but my father and three older brothers 
loved me with everything they had.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:06.540
Father! Brothers! I want to be a knight!

00:10:08.230 --> 00:10:10.760
They did not approve of my dream.

00:10:14.510 --> 00:10:17.470
If I was successful as a Hunter, 
I could become a knight.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.190
I ran away from home.

00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:21.530
And now!

00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.800
I am here!

00:10:25.980 --> 00:10:28.310
Stop giving me those, "Is that all?" looks!

00:10:29.060 --> 00:10:32.560
I'm starting to feel stupid for 
thinking so hard about all of this.

00:10:32.560 --> 00:10:34.150
Is that my fault?

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:38.230
Thank goodness! Mavis-san's simple 
past was good for something, then!

00:10:38.230 --> 00:10:40.780
You don't have to be so 
casually blunt about it, Mile!

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:44.330
Now, then. It's time for our main event.

00:10:44.330 --> 00:10:45.120
Huh?

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:47.780
Stare...

00:10:47.780 --> 00:10:52.160
No, but before, Pauline-san said I didn't 
have to say anything if I didn't want to!

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.650
Indeed I did, but don't you 
want to talk about it now?

00:10:59.680 --> 00:11:00.780
All right.

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:03.230
I'll tell you the truth.

00:11:05.400 --> 00:11:09.160
My real name is Adele von Ascham.

00:11:09.160 --> 00:11:12.980
I'm the daughter of Viscount 
Ascham of the Brandel Kingdom.

00:11:13.170 --> 00:11:15.110
You're a noble?

00:11:15.350 --> 00:11:16.480
Technically, yes...

00:11:16.480 --> 00:11:18.110
We'll start the flashback here,

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:22.360
but for Reina-dono and the others, we'll be
 leaving out anything about reincarnation.

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:25.740
The day I turned ten,

00:11:25.920 --> 00:11:29.370
I regained my memories from my previous life.

00:11:29.660 --> 00:11:32.050
My name is Kurihara Misato...

00:11:32.510 --> 00:11:33.520
No...

00:11:33.520 --> 00:11:34.600
Adele.

00:11:36.240 --> 00:11:38.130
I really reincarnated!

00:11:38.690 --> 00:11:40.920
I was the daughter of a Viscount.

00:11:40.920 --> 00:11:43.890
If you're wondering why I'm a noble 
when I asked for "average"...

